 "_notes": [
  "Chaos Dwarfs 3.0 (Mathias Eliasson). Scope: Core / Special / Rare only — no characters, no special characters. Source: data/chaos-dwarfs.js.",
  "save = final armour save ROLL after combining armour + shield (7 - total modifier). Light +1, Medium +2, Heavy +3, Shield +1, Natural Armour(X+) = 7-X and STACKS with worn armour.",
  "Great weapon in 9th Ed 3.0 = S+1 with Mighty Blow (1): so S+2 in the FIRST round and S+1 sustained — NOT a flat +2. Great-weapon units get two builds, (1st round) and (sustained).",
  "Black Orcs have their own Mighty Blow (1); with a great weapon that stacks to Mighty Blow (2), so first round = base +1 (GW strength) +2 (both Mighty Blows) = +3, sustained = +1.",
  "Fireglaive = +1 Strength in combat (two hands); shooting S5 9/18\" Ponderous.",
  "Blackshard Armour (Infernal Guard, Immortals) grants Immunity (Flaming Attacks) — no effect on these benchmarks, not modelled.",
  "Contempt / Relentless / Resolute: Resolute -> hold 'resolute' (counts a lost combat as 1 less). Immortals are Stubborn; K'daai / Iron Daemon / Juggernaut / Kolossus are Unbreakable (Kolossus via Animated Construct).",
  "Daemonic (K'daai) = Magical Ward (5+) + Unbreakable -> ward:5, hold:'daemonic'. Hellbound (Kolossus) = Magical Ward (6+). Natural Armour is a real save; ward is unmodified by Strength.",
  "Monsters get Stomp (D6)=3.5 auto-hits at their own Strength vs targets with Line of Sight <= 3 (K'daai Destroyer, Kolossus). Iron Daemon's Grind Attack is the same Stomp when it does not charge.",
  "Multiple Wounds is counted uncapped (wounds inflicted, not models killed): D3 -> mw 2, D6 -> mw 3.5.",
  "War-machine template hit-counts (Magma, Deathshrieker, Dreadquake, Hellcannon doomfire) and organ-gun/steam-cannonade shot-counts are STATED ESTIMATES — they swing with scatter and misfire.",
  "Reliability (Hold/ADJ) columns are omitted here to match the other army files, but UNLIKE Daemons the CD hold factor genuinely varies (Ld 3-10, Stubborn, Unbreakable, Treacherous Gits). Run the skill with --reliability to separate anchors from chaff.",
  "Warriors + Infernal Cohort: heavy armour upgrade (+1.5/model, one unit per Despot) -> heavy+shield = 3+ save at 9.5 pts; included because it is the cheapest 3+ body in the book, but note it requires a Despot in the list.",
  "Deliberate omissions: Killing Blow (none core), Blunderbuss/Bolt Throwa exact profiles approximated, Siege Giant's random '*' attacks not modelled (resilience only), command/magic-standard and the other character-dependent host upgrades (Granite Guard, Ironsworn, Ravagers, Blazing Beards) excluded."
 ],
